hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2809","**\nNarrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Walid, narrated to us Yazid. And narrated to us Muhammad ibn Yahya, narrated to us Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Nufayli, narrated to us Hatim ibn Isma'il, narrated to us Ja'far ibn Muhammad, on the authority of his father, who said:\n\nWe entered upon Jabir ibn Abdullah, who mentioned the hadith and said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) proceeded until he reached 'Arafah. When the sun declined, he ordered that the she-camel al-Qaswa' be saddled for him, and he mounted it until he reached the bottom of the valley. There he addressed the people and said:\n\n\Indeed"","" your blood"","" your wealth"","" and your honour are sacred to one another as the sanctity of this day of yours"","" in this month of yours"","" in this city of yours. Behold! Every practice of the Days of Ignorance is beneath my feet"","" and the bloodshed of the Days of Ignorance is remitted. The first blood I remit is that of Ibn Rabi'ah ibn al-Harith"","" who was nursed among the Banu Sa'd"","" and was killed by Hudhayl.\n\nAnd the usury of the Days of Ignorance is remitted. The first usury I remit is that of al-'Abbas ibn 'Abd al-Muttalib; it is all remitted.\n\nFear Allah concerning women"","" for you have taken them as a trust from Allah"","" and intimacy with them has been made lawful to you by the word of Allah. You have rights over them that they should not allow anyone you dislike to sit on your beds. If they do that"","" then strike them lightly without causing injury.\n\nThey have rights over you that you should provide them with food and clothing in a reasonable manner.\n\nI have left among you something which"","" if you hold fast to it"","" you will never go astray: the Book of Allah. And you will be questioned about me"","" so what will you say?\""\n\nThey said: \""We bear witness that you have conveyed the messages of your Lord"","" advised your nation"","" and fulfilled what was upon you.\""\n\nHe (ﷺ) then raised his forefinger towards the sky and moved it towards the people"","" saying: \""O Allah"","" bear witness! O Allah"","" bear witness!\""\n\nAbu Bakr (RA) said: I have explained in the chapter on marriage that his statement"","" \""they should not allow anyone you dislike to sit on your beds"",""\"" means the act of placing the feet on the bed"","" as the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""No one should sit on his honour (takrimah) except with his permission"",""\"" and the bed of a man is his honour. He did not mean what the ignorant people imagine"","" namely sexual intercourse."""""
